  "cues": [
    {
      "start": 0.325,
      "end": 3.573,
      "text": "Imagine building one of the world's most loved toy brands\u2026"
    },
    {
      "start": 4.025,
      "end": 5.81,
      "text": "then almost losing everything."
    },
    {
      "start": 8.314,
      "end": 12.012,
      "text": "By 2004, LEGO was in its worst financial crisis."
    },
    {
      "start": 12.167,
      "end": 13.688,
      "text": "Its business had become complicated,"
    },
    {
      "start": 13.808,
      "end": 16.702,
      "text": "expensive, and increasingly difficult to manage."
    },
    {
      "start": 16.873,
      "end": 20.719,
      "text": "That year, it reported a net loss of nearly two billion Danish kroner."
    },
    {
      "start": 21.231,
      "end": 24.099,
      "text": "LEGO had expanded into too many directions."
    },
    {
      "start": 24.31,
      "end": 26.981,
      "text": "More products, more complexity, more costs."
    },
    {
      "start": 27.161,
      "end": 28.964,
      "text": "It was trying to become everything,"
    },
    {
      "start": 29.105,
      "end": 31.545,
      "text": "while losing focus on what made it special."
    },
    {
      "start": 32.107,
      "end": 33.676,
      "text": "Then came a major change."
    },
    {
      "start": 33.848,
      "end": 37.178,
      "text": "In 2004, J\u00f8rgen Vig Knudstorp became CEO."
    },
    {
      "start": 37.368,
      "end": 40.505,
      "text": "His mission wasn't to make LEGO bigger in every direction."
    },
    {
      "start": 40.68,
      "end": 42.601,
      "text": "It was to make the business stronger."
    },
    {
      "start": 43.331,
      "end": 45.829,
      "text": "LEGO started cutting unnecessary complexity,"
    },
    {
      "start": 46.143,
      "end": 49.139,
      "text": "selling non-core assets, reducing costs,"
    },
    {
      "start": 49.269,
      "end": 52.6,
      "text": "and returning its attention to its core product: the brick."
    },
    {
      "start": 52.81,
      "end": 55.968,
      "text": "It also worked to reconnect with the customers who loved it."
    },
    {
      "start": 57.305,
      "end": 58.583,
      "text": "The turnaround worked."
    },
    {
      "start": 58.774,
      "end": 63.117000000000004,
      "text": "By 2015, LEGO's revenue had reached 35.8 billion"
    },
    {
      "start": 63.237,
      "end": 64.099,
      "text": "Danish kroner."
    },
    {
      "start": 64.289,
      "end": 66.44999999999999,
      "text": "A company that had once faced a serious fight for"
    },
    {
      "start": 66.57,
      "end": 70.656,
      "text": "survival had rebuilt itself into one of the world's leading toy businesses."
    },
    {
      "start": 71.325,
      "end": 74.621,
      "text": "Here's the lesson: growth isn't always about doing more."
    },
    {
      "start": 74.777,
      "end": 77.362,
      "text": "Sometimes, it's about getting back to what you do best."
    }
  ]
}
